flowchart LR
  conv[("Seeded conventions")]
  subgraph cli["Agent CLI"]
    direction TB
    claude["Claude"]
    codex["Codex"]
    opencode["OpenCode"]
    antigravity["Antigravity"]
    others["others"]
    claude ~~~ codex ~~~ opencode ~~~ antigravity ~~~ others
  end
  guard["bram-guard"]
  host["Bram host"]
  tx[("Turn records")]
  state[("State folder")]

  conv -->|"loaded each session"| cli
  host -->|"launches, answers menus"| cli
  cli -->|"each tool call"| guard
  guard -->|"allow or deny"| cli
  guard -->|"reads coverage"| state
  cli -->|"resolve, mutate, commit, end"| host
  host -->|"writes"| state
  cli -->|"each turn"| tx
  tx -->|"read for turn state and the Transcript"| host

%% tip: Seeded conventions :: app/__shell/conventions.md and its reference files, copied into the project by Setup. Each provider loads them by its own channel; following them is up to the model.
%% tip: Claude :: Claude Code, the claude command, launched with a session id Bram reserves.
%% tip: Codex :: Codex CLI, launched with --no-daemon when its help lists it.
%% tip: OpenCode :: OpenCode, launched --standalone so its plugin carries this Bram's token.
%% tip: Antigravity :: Antigravity CLI, the agy command, with AGY_CLI_OSC7501=on so it reports turn state.
%% tip: others :: Not a provider yet. A fifth one is another wrapped CLI on the same flows; Cursor has a specimen pack.
%% tip: bram-guard :: One Rust binary with four registrations (claude-worklist, codex-worklist, opencode-worklist, antigravity-worklist), all reaching the same decider.
%% tip: Bram host :: The Rust process: launches each CLI, serves the loopback routes, reads the turn records, and shows the pane.
%% tip: Turn records :: Where each provider writes its turns: Claude's JSONL, Codex's rollouts, OpenCode's SQLite and plugin events, agy's store projected by Bram.
%% tip: State folder :: resources/ (or .bram/ once it exists): the worklist, drafts, the authorization record, the claim, traces.
%% tip: loaded each session :: CLAUDE.md import; the AGENTS.md block and Codex developer instructions; opencode.json instructions; always-on rules in .agents/rules.
%% tip: launches, answers menus :: claude with a session id; codex --no-daemon; opencode --standalone so its events carry this Bram's token; agy with AGY_CLI_OSC7501=on; menu hooks, the plugin, or agy's screen-read dialogs.
%% tip: each tool call :: A hook in .claude/settings.local.json; a hook in ~/.codex/config.toml; the .opencode/plugins plugin; the hook group in .agents/hooks.json.
%% tip: allow or deny :: The decision goes back as the hook's exit or the plugin's throw; the Antigravity payload is shape-checked and fails closed.
%% tip: reads coverage :: The guard reads worklist.json and the authorization record from the state folder to decide whether an edit is covered.
%% tip: resolve, mutate, commit, end :: Loopback curl for Claude, OpenCode and Antigravity; intent and result files for Codex, whose sandbox refuses loopback.
%% tip: writes :: The host writes the worklist, the authorization record, the claim, the history and the traces.
%% tip: each turn :: JSONL under ~/.claude/projects; rollouts under ~/.codex/sessions; SQLite plus plugin events; agy's records under ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli, exported by Bram.
%% tip: read for turn state and the Transcript :: Hook events for Claude; rollout mtime for Codex; plugin events for OpenCode; OSC 7501 state and screen-read menus for Antigravity. All project into one Transcript.
